Bots filled into an LFG group are re-attempted every 5 seconds until they
reach the dungeon, instead of dying quietly with the group unfilled.

Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.{h,cpp}
         (new UpdateLfgFillTeleports, ProcessLfgFillTeleports deadline 600s)
         modules/mod-playerbots/src/Script/Playerbots.cpp
         (PlayerbotsScript::OnUpdate calls UpdateLfgFillTeleports)
No tracked src/server/ files change -- no core diff in this record; it
documents gitignored module edits.

Why: report #165 / issue (fill-teleport follow-up to #149/#151) -- "playerbots
still not teleporting into dungeons immediately via LFD, need to have it
retry every 5 seconds until they're in party range of the character".

Two stacked causes, one per fix:

1. CADENCE. The retry pass (ProcessLfgFillTeleports, from 0041) ran from
   RandomPlayerbotMgr::UpdateAIInternal, whose pass re-arms at
   randomBotUpdateInterval * (onlineBotFocus + 25) * 10 ms -- 30-60s in the
   live config. The old 10s deadline (later bumped to 90s in the working
   tree, never built) usually saw ZERO or one attempt before expiry; live
   evidence: 48 "LFG fill teleport expired" vs 13 delivered in five hours,
   with the big fills (10/25-man) losing every bot. UpdateLfgFillTeleports
   is now called from PlayerbotsScript::OnUpdate -- every world tick -- and
   internally spaces attempts 5s apart (lfgFillTeleportRetryAt), exactly as
   the report asks. The UpdateAIInternal call is gone; its comment explains
   why it must not come back.

2. WINDOW. The deadline is 600s. Entries drop on arrival (bot's map == the
   group dungeon's map -- the entrance square MakeNewGroup put the party on,
   i.e. "in party range"), on logout, or when the group stops being an LFG
   group, so the list cannot leak; the deadline only bounds a bot that
   genuinely cannot go for the whole window (dead and never revived,
   endless combat). The guards still mirror LFGMgr::TeleportPlayer's
   refusals: dead, combat, falling, mid-teleport, charmed, fatigued bots
   are re-attempted on the next 5s pass, not dropped.
